  m_text: "The statue, carved by Jos\xE9 Montes de Oca in the 1730s captures Saint
    Benedict's charismatic personality. Alongside the glass eyes and bone teeth,
    it adds saint's life like quality. \n\nAdditionally, the statue's capture of
    Benedict's concentrated expression, open arms and his symmetrical stance brings
    out what Saint Benedict was to everyone during his life on Earth. \n\nA protector."
